===Etymology 4===
{{ja-kanjitab|みち|yomi=k|alt=路:uncommon,途:rare,径:rare}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|-|sort=みち}}, ultimately from {{inh|ja|jpx-pro|*miti|sort=みち}}.

Originally a compound of {{ja-com|sort=みち|御|み-|pos1=honorific prefix|路|ち|t2=[[road]], [[street]], [[way]]}}.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref> The prefix ''mi-'' was in reference to the {{ja-r|神|かみ|[[god]], [[spirit]]}} of roads.

Perhaps also cognate with {{IPAfont|*miti}}, a potentially road-related element found in Old Korean toponyms.<ref>{{cite-journal|first=Alexander|last=Vovin|authorlink=Alexander Vovin|title=From Koguryo to T'amna|year=2013|journal=Korean Linguistics|volume=15|issue=2|publisher=John Benjamins Publishing Company|doi=10.1075/kl.15.2.03vov|pages=222-240|url=https://www.academia.edu/6360018/From_Koguryo_to_Tamna|format=PDF}}.</ref>

